  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_b569ec80021646e894f1b5801e36a631",
      "statement": "Residency is a hard cap (CELLD_MAX_RESIDENT_CELLS) enforced at admission, while memory pressure is a separate resource-aware classifier; CELLD_ACTIVATIONS separately bounds concurrent nonresident cold routes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L3-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0dd600768a3c2d7976136d9049625b51436ee370a877bd530077dec64a929bad:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L63-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d3926781b6db853c390d374da26349f76bc07c5e9ad75e5dd297230eb35f916a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_723c272cc430433c9f5a9cd26403cc02",
      "statement": "The ordinary pressure measurement is the greater of allocator-adjusted RSS and the allocator-adjusted active cgroup working set (memory.current minus inactive_file), while the hard measurement is the complete memory.current charge with process RSS as a fallback.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/memory.rs#L3-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4d3e212d5d587a3a6138aaa156459deba8fd3b9da74b93866cdaf3684f288100:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L95-L114",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d645680f9faf5f70cc9cb63a293c89f487fde63cc26a4502f4bdc9d57f68e251:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_04bb0d1f93684c1f942232680dd76512",
      "statement": "The allocator adjustment subtracts the pages jemalloc keeps but no cell uses (stats.resident less stats.allocated), so a node that sheds its whole working set is not latched on an RSS number the allocator controls.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/memory.rs#L164-L178",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1bf3a3c0239a48af838cec2ccf071d30145faab234262bddd9ec7d5b3ae19485:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ecbabcf82f7d4d3292a6cbc2e9019387",
      "statement": "The pressure ceilings are built from the machine and CELLD_MAX_RSS_MB: the ordinary ceiling defaults to 80% of available memory, the absolute cap is 95% of the machine (never derived from the ceiling, falling back to 125% of an explicit ceiling when the machine size is unknown), and CELLD_MAX_RSS_MB=0 disables pressure shedding.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L133-L177",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bbe7d8aee9df159aaaa1f857d10663f3100f5c17f35eac6f122e8f1bb84b47b5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L179-L190",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8b068bb807e9da8136c387409bfa4b49302ddc86b1b32626b4675569e0897db8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0d3d13630ef34f95ab17b5834a9ed353",
      "statement": "Each pressure ceiling latches at its own ceiling and releases at its own low watermark of 80% of that ceiling, with the latches carried separately so one crossing cannot hold the node against the other's watermark.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L192-L230",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b90a390fb1e4a8a48db1d18f2efd0b884df782ef5d5573058bf2589ee940924c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_014d0a92a423462b878919bd27e774f5",
      "statement": "Under pressure the node evicts least-recently used idle cells after proving their replicas durable, publishes them unowned without resetting their epochs, and refuses to reacquire new unowned cells; the walk targets 80% of the latched ceiling so it stops rather than cutting the working set to zero.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L288-L295",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ad47775468603a7b7e1d811947b44eec7201d818d58e8ea83a274429c3673ec2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L4696-L4730",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c737f3743d585bf6fdcc427dd749bcecaf644470ec50cd85d027b50897c1c6e3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1b11960aaf054c3b93e29f405744806c",
      "statement": "A node over its memory ceiling may keep serving on its existing isolates but must not build another, except when there is nothing to place onto.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/isolate.rs#L144-L163",
